    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nAn idyllic thatched cottage with stunning sea views along the Wild Atlantic Way\n\nBumblebee Cottage is a charming thatched cottage, dating from about 1860, set on an elevated site overlooking Fintra Beach near Killybegs. From its elevated position on the side of the hill, the cottage enjoys uninterrupted panoramic views across Donegal Bay, extending to the Sligo coastline with Ben Bulben visible in the distance.\n\nApproached via a quiet country lane, the property sits within a gravel forecourt and driveway. Bumblebee Cottage represents a rare surviving example of Donegal's vernacular heritage, combining architectural authenticity with modern usability in a truly scenic setting.\n\nThe property retains much of its original character and form. A scallop-thatched rye straw roof complete with new ropes has been recently installed, in keeping with south-west Donegal's roofing tradition, giving the cottage a new golden glow. \n\nInternally, the home has been tastefully renovated to balance heritage and comfort. Reclaimed timber flooring and a handcrafted sandstone fireplace anchor the open-plan living and kitchen area, which features bespoke cabinetry, a Belfast sink, and vaulted ceilings with exposed beams. There is an extension to the side of the cottage with a utility /goods storage room. \n\nAccommodation includes two bedrooms, one currently set up as an office, and one bathroom, all thoughtfully arranged to maximise space and natural light. There is also scope to extend the cottage to the rear and to the side (subject to the necessary planning permission) with indicative plans available on request from the selling agents. \n\nThe total internal area extends to approximately 576 sq ft (53.5 sq m), as shown in the accompanying floorplans.\n\nGardens & Grounds\n\nThe property sits on private grounds, offering a sheltered setting with mature planting and space for outdoor living. A gravel driveway provides access and parking, while the land to the rear frames the cottage beautifully, creating a tranquil retreat with panoramic views. In addition, the area below the cottage presents an opportunity for further landscaping or other uses (subject to the necessary planning permission). \n\nIn all the grounds extend to about 0.5 acre / 0.21 hectare.\n\nGeneral Remarks\n\nViewing\nStrictly by private appointment with the sole selling agents Savills Country.\n\nEircode\nF94 HY43\n\nFixtures & Fittings\nAll fixtures and fittings are excluded from the sale including garden statuary, light fittings, and other removable fittings, although some items may be available by separate negotiation.\n\nServices\nOil Fired Central Heating (tank installed in 2023), mains water, mains electricity, septic tank, internet connectivity currently via Starlink.\n\nPlease be advised that the selling agents have not checked the services and any purchaser should satisfy themselves with the availability and adequacy of all services.\n\nEntry & Possession\nEntry is by agreement with vacant possession.\n\nOffers\nOffers may be submitted to the sole selling agents Savills Country.\n\nBest Offers Date\nA date for best offers may be fixed and prospective purchasers are asked to register their interest with the sole selling agents following inspection. The sellers reserve the right to exchange a Contract for the sale of any part of the subjects of sale ahead of a notified closing date and will not be obliged to accept the highest or any offer.\n\nFinancial Guarantee\nAll offers (regardless of the country of residence of the offering party) must be accompanied by a guarantee or suitable form of reference from a bank, which gives the sellers satisfaction that the purchaser has access to the funds required to complete the purchase at the offered price.\n\nWayleaves and Rights of Access\nThe property will be sold with the benefit of all existing wayleave rights, including rights of access and rights of way, whether public or private. The purchaser will be held to have satisfied themselves as to the nature of all such rights and others.\n\nGenerally\nShould there be any discrepancy between these particulars, the General Remarks and Information, Stipulations and the Contract of Sale, the latter shall prevail."
      },
